how/136248346.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-28T19:14:03+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rohitashwa Ranjan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136248555,imgsize-99616.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Final call in day or two’: India-bloc ally JMM to decide stand on delimitation, women's quota Bills after assessing impact on Jharkhand]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/final-call-in-day-or-two-india-bloc-ally-jmm-to-decide-stand-on-delimitation-womens-quota-bills-after-assessing-impact-on-jharkhand/articleshow/136248323.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136248323.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Jharkhand Mukti Morcha (JMM) plans to analyze the proposed delimitation and women's reservation Bills shortly. A recent meeting with JMM MPs was chaired by Chief Minister Hemant Soren to discuss these Bills. The party aims to evaluate the impact of the legislation on Scheduled Tribes seats in Jharkhand. Various opposition parties have differing views on these proposed measures surrounding social justice and representation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/final-call-in-day-or-two-india-bloc-ally-jmm-to-decide-stand-on-delimitation-womens-quota-bills-after-assessing-impact-on-jharkhand/articleshow/136248323.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/final-call-in-day-or-two-india-bloc-ally-jmm-to-decide-stand-on-delimitation-womens-quota-bills-after-assessing-impact-on-jharkhand/articleshow/136248323.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-28T19:11:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136248527,imgsize-1230593.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[From Dali to Picasso, a 23-year-old's mission to bring European art to India]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/from-dali-to-picasso-a-23-year-olds-mission-to-bring-european-art-to-india/articleshow/136248004.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136248004.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/from-dali-to-picasso-a-23-year-olds-mission-to-bring-european-art-to-india/articleshow/136248004.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/from-dali-to-picasso-a-23-year-olds-mission-to-bring-european-art-to-india/articleshow/136248004.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-28T18:49:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sneha Bhura</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136248093,imgsize-83820.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Vetrivel, Veeravel': Historic lighting of Deepam, emotional celebrations captured in 9 videos]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/vetrivel-veeravel-historic-lighting-of-deepam-emotional-celebrations-captured-in-9-videos/articleshow/136246533.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136246533.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[On Saturday, Madurai devotees witnessed the lighting of the Karthigai Deepam at Thiruparankundram hill. This ceremony took place under the supervision of Supreme Court-appointed judges. A significant gathering celebrated the event while following strict security measures and guidelines. A devotee expressed concerns over previous noncompliance with the Supreme Court's orders. Prime Minister Narendra Modi also acknowledged the occasion in a social media post.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/vetrivel-veeravel-historic-lighting-of-deepam-emotional-celebrations-captured-in-9-videos/articleshow/136246533.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/vetrivel-veeravel-historic-lighting-of-deepam-emotional-celebrations-captured-in-9-videos/articleshow/136246533.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-28T18:24:05+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136247527,imgsize-19702920.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Police use water cannon on Congress workers protesting outside Meta office]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/police-use-water-cannon-on-congress-workers-protesting-outside-meta-office/articleshow/136247015.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136247015.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/police-use-water-cannon-on-congress-workers-protesting-outside-meta-office/articleshow/136247015.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/police-use-water-cannon-on-congress-workers-protesting-outside-meta-office/articleshow/136247015.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-28T18:19:48+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Priyanka Jaiswal</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136247439,imgsize-165650.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A wall across the sea: Inside Gujarat's ambitious Kalpasar project]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/a-wall-across-the-sea-inside-gujarats-ambitious-kalpasar-project/articleshow/136243260.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136243260.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Gujarat is embarking on an ambitious project to build a 60.13-km barrier across the Gulf of Khambhat to create a freshwater reservoir. This initiative will harness runoff from multiple rivers, enhancing connectivity and supporting energy infrastructure. However, experts warn of significant engineering and environmental challenges, highlighting potential risks to marine life and water quality. The project's triumph hinges on meticulous planning and thorough investigations prior to execution.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/a-wall-across-the-sea-inside-gujarats-ambitious-kalpasar-project/articleshow/136243260.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/a-wall-across-the-sea-inside-gujarats-ambitious-kalpasar-project/articleshow/136243260.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-28T18:18:05+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aryan Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136243344,imgsize-266084.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Blank cheque to redraw electoral map to BJP's advantage': Rahul Gandhi on delimitation bill - top quotes]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/blank-cheque-to-redraw-electoral-map-to-bjps-advantage-rahul-gandhi-on-delimitation-bill-top-quotes/articleshow/136247216.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136247216.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/blank-cheque-to-redraw-electoral-map-to-bjps-advantage-rahul-gandhi-on-delimitation-bill-top-quotes/articleshow/136247216.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/blank-cheque-to-redraw-electoral-map-to-bjps-advantage-rahul-gandhi-on-delimitation-bill-top-quotes/articleshow/136247216.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-28T18:14:04+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rohitashwa Ranjan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136247259,imgsize-38480.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Post-Delimitation:  What the new Lok Sabha will look like — in infographic]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/post-delimitation-what-the-new-lok-sabha-will-look-like-in-infographic/articleshow/136244003.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136244003.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Union law minister Arjun Ram Meghwal announced the proposed expansion of Lok Sabha seats to 816 by 2029. Uttar Pradesh is set to gain the highest number of seats, rising from 80 to 120. The initiative also aims to implement 33 percent reservation for women in Parliament to enhance their representation. Several states, including Maharashtra, Bihar, and West Bengal, will also see significant increases in their seat allocations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/post-delimitation-what-the-new-lok-sabha-will-look-like-in-infographic/articleshow/136244003.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/post-delimitation-what-the-new-lok-sabha-will-look-like-in-infographic/articleshow/136244003.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-28T18:00:08+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136244227,imgsize-228070.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Evening news wrap: Deepam lit on deepathoon, SC clears way for Hockey India polls &amp; more]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/evening-news-wrap-deepam-lit-on-deepathoon-sc-clears-way-for-hockey-india-polls-more/articleshow/136246440.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136246440.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/evening-news-wrap-deepam-lit-on-deepathoon-sc-clears-way-for-hockey-india-polls-more/articleshow/136246440.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/evening-news-wrap-deepam-lit-on-deepathoon-sc-clears-way-for-hockey-india-polls-more/articleshow/136246440.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-28T17:55:13+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136246864,imgsize-154560.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[NIA launches probe into Myanmar-based armed groups' terror links in Manipur]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/nia-launches-probe-into-myanmar-based-armed-groups-terror-links-in-manipur/articleshow/136246339.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136246339.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/nia-launches-probe-into-myanmar-based-armed-groups-terror-links-in-manipur/articleshow/136246339.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/nia-launches-probe-into-myanmar-based-armed-groups-terror-links-in-manipur/articleshow/136246339.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-28T17:33:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rohitashwa Ranjan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136246368,imgsize-72946.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[JD(U) extends full support to delimitation, women's reservation proposals]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jdu-extends-full-support-to-delimitation-womens-reservation-proposals/articleshow/136245095.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136245095.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The Janata Dal (United) has voiced its endorsement for the upcoming Constitution amendment bills focused on delimitation and women's reservation. These proposals aim to expand the representation in both Lok Sabha and state assemblies, ensuring that women secure 33 percent of the seats. The BJP-led central government is set to present these amendments in the Lok Sabha shortly.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jdu-extends-full-support-to-delimitation-womens-reservation-proposals/articleshow/136245095.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jdu-extends-full-support-to-delimitation-womens-reservation-proposals/articleshow/136245095.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-28T17:01:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136245602,imgsize-76350.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Gen Z, farmers angry; BJP losing UP': Akhilesh says Centre using delimitation to divert attention]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/gen-z-farmers-angry-bjp-losing-up-akhilesh-says-centre-using-delimitation-to-divert-attention/articleshow/136245135.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136245135.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/gen-z-farmers-angry-bjp-losing-up-akhilesh-says-centre-using-delimitation-to-divert-attention/articleshow/136245135.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/gen-z-farmers-angry-bjp-losing-up-akhilesh-says-centre-using-delimitation-to-divert-attention/articleshow/136245135.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-28T16:52:49+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Priyanka Jaiswal</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136245357,imgsize-92419.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[President Murmu clears key procedural step for tabling of revised Delimitation Bill in Parliament]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/president-murmu-clears-key-procedural-step-for-tabling-of-revised-delimitation-bill-in-parliament/articleshow/136245031.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136245031.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[President Droupadi Murmu has recommended that the Lok Sabha consider the Delimitation (Second) Bill, 2026. This recommendation is essential for the legislative process to proceed effectively. The Lok Sabha is scheduled to meet between November 30 and December 3 to discuss the proposal. The revised package outlines a 50 percent increase in seats for the Lok Sabha and state Assemblies.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/president-murmu-clears-key-procedural-step-for-tabling-of-revised-delimitation-bill-in-parliament/articleshow/136245031.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/president-murmu-clears-key-procedural-step-for-tabling-of-revised-delimitation-bill-in-parliament/articleshow/136245031.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-28T16:48:29+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136245246,imgsize-86276.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[CM Shivakumar warns of 'Delhi Chalo' stir if Centre continues to withhold drought aid]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cm-shivakumar-warns-of-delhi-chalo-stir-if-centre-continues-to-withhold-drought-aid/articleshow/136244343.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136244343.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cm-shivakumar-warns-of-delhi-chalo-stir-if-centre-continues-to-withhold-drought-aid/articleshow/136244343.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cm-shivakumar-warns-of-delhi-chalo-stir-if-centre-continues-to-withhold-drought-aid/articleshow/136244343.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-28T16:28:30+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Priyanka Jaiswal</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136244343,imgsize-801801.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Odisha to host National conference on AI in litigation on December 12-13]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/odisha-to-host-national-conference-on-ai-in-litigation-on-december-12-13/articleshow/136244430.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136244430.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[On December 12 and 13, Odisha will be the site of a groundbreaking two-day conference focused on artificial intelligence's impact on litigation. Senior judicial figures, including the Chief Justice of India, are set to join approximately 300 delegates. Discussions will revolve around AI's role within India's legal framework, technological advancements, and how they influence court procedures, from digital courts to AI-driven translations and virtual hearings.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/odisha-to-host-national-conference-on-ai-in-litigation-on-december-12-13/articleshow/136244430.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/odisha-to-host-national-conference-on-ai-in-litigation-on-december-12-13/articleshow/136244430.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-28T16:26:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136244839,imgsize-92242.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Did not prioritise family planning': Javed Akhtar questions seat distribution under delimitation]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/did-not-prioritise-family-planning-javed-akhtar-questions-seat-distribution-under-delimitation/articleshow/136244708.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136244708.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Javed Akhtar expressed concerns regarding the proposed delimitation Bill and its implications for Lok Sabha seat allocation. He criticized the plan for potentially favoring states that did not prioritize family planning. The Union Cabinet approved revised legislations for the delimitation process and women's reservation in Parliament. Opposition parties have supported women's reservation but opposed linking it to the delimitation exercise.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/did-not-prioritise-family-planning-javed-akhtar-questions-seat-distribution-under-delimitation/articleshow/136244708.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/did-not-prioritise-family-planning-javed-akhtar-questions-seat-distribution-under-delimitation/articleshow/136244708.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-28T16:22:17+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136244765,imgsize-42606.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Mortgaging self-respect': Raut takes aim at Sharad Pawar's NCP over delimitation bill]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/mortgaging-self-respect-raut-takes-aim-at-sharad-pawars-ncp-over-delimitation-bill/articleshow/136243966.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136243966.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Sanjay Raut alleged that BJP engineered a split within the Nationalist Congress Party and the Pawar family. He expressed concerns that supporting the proposed delimitation bill would compromise the NCP's self-respect and contradict its ideological principles. Raut emphasized that the NCP's MPs had won their seats without BJP support and should acknowledge this. He criticized the bill as a political maneuver to favor the BJP ahead of the upcoming elections.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/mortgaging-self-respect-raut-takes-aim-at-sharad-pawars-ncp-over-delimitation-bill/articleshow/136243966.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/mortgaging-self-respect-raut-takes-aim-at-sharad-pawars-ncp-over-delimitation-bill/articleshow/136243966.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-28T16:16:45+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136244617,imgsize-34030.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Modi is not going anywhere': Rajnath hits back at Congress, says only people can remove PM]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/modi-is-not-going-anywhere-rajnath-hits-back-at-congress-says-only-people-can-remove-pm/articleshow/136243975.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136243975.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/modi-is-not-going